{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "moves.fuel_effects",
    "description": "Template library: the algebraic FORMS of `FuelEffectsGenerator.doGeneralFuelRatio`'s `fuelEffectRatioExpression` column. Ports crates/moves-calculators/src/generators/fueleffectsgenerator/{expression,generalfuelratio}.rs, which port gov/epa/otaq/moves/master/implementation/ghg/FuelEffectsGenerator.java. Specified in docs/fuel-effects-generator.md.\n\nWHY THIS FILE IS TEMPLATES AND NOT A TABLE. MOVES keeps these equations in a VARCHAR column: `generalFuelRatioExpression.fuelEffectRatioExpression` holds SQL arithmetic that the Java pastes into `select (EXPRESSION) from fuelFormulation` and MariaDB evaluates. That is the same category of thing an `.esm` expression is, and docs/esm-conventions.md 24 settles what to do with it -- the FORMS become expression templates, spelled once, and the per-row COEFFICIENTS stay data. Measured over the whole snapshot corpus: 2,078 expression-table rows, 567 distinct rows, 118 distinct expression strings, and 72 distinct parse-tree skeletons -- which collapse to SIX top-level algebraic forms plus a bare constant, three of which are ported here. Those counts are dated (the corpus grew by two captures while this rung was being verified and moved every one of them by 15 to 20 %); the SIX did not move, which is the practical argument for factoring. docs/fuel-effects-generator.md 7.5 has the before-and-after. docs/fuel-effects-generator.md 2 has the census and 8.1 says why the other three are not.\n\nTHE THREE FORMS PORTED HERE.\n\n* `log_linear_ratio` -- `exp(SUM)/base`, where SUM is a sum of `standardized_term`s over centred and scaled fuel properties. 32 rows, 2 distinct strings, in one snapshot. This is the form the reference checks: 32 of the 97 compared rows.\n* `biodiesel_ester_ratio` -- `1 + (least(bioDieselEsterVolume, 20)/100)*coefficient`. 676 rows, 4 distinct strings, and 65 of the 97 compared rows. Its four coefficients are the whole of its per-row data.\n* `sulfur_switch_ratio` -- `if(sulfurLevel > 30, HIGH, LOW)`, the criteria fuel model. 1,013 rows and 100 distinct strings -- 57 distinct parse-tree skeletons between them, which is term ORDER and not form -- the corpus's dominant form. NOT ONE of its rows is checked against MOVES through `generalFuelRatio`, because `doCOCalculations`, `doHCCalculations` and `doNOxCalculations` copy every one of them into `criteriaRatio` and delete them from `generalFuelRatio` before the snapshot is taken -- so it is checked through `criteriaRatio` instead, which is where they went: `onroad/model.esm` evaluates this form for the criteria running-exhaust pollutant-processes and `runspecs/pending/expand-criteria.esm` lands 309 of its 372 cells at a worst 7.804e-06 (docs/fuel-effects-generator.md 8.1). It is ported because the algebra is the same algebra a later criteriaRatio rung needs, and every assertion that reaches it in components/fuel_effects.esm says, in the test, that it faces THIS PORT and a second independent evaluation of the same MOVES string -- never the reference (docs/esm-conventions.md 35.4).\n\nWHY `standardized_term` CARRIES A POWER AND A CAP. Both are in the strings. `least(10, ETOHVolume)` appears wherever an E85 expression clamps the ethanol volume before centring it -- the E85 rows are the only ones that do, and the clamp is written as a term-level cap here rather than as a second copy of the form. `T50*T50` appears in the criteria polynomial, so a term carries an exponent; every other term's is 1, and `pow(x, 1)` is exactly `x`. Writing the two variants as separate templates would be docs/esm-conventions.md 6's repetition, and folding the cap into the data as a sentinel would need a magic large number -- `cap_is_active` is an indicator for the same reason components/meteorology.esm's `pressure_is_present` is one.\n\nTHE POWERS ARE `exp(g*ln(x))` AND NOT `x^g`, DELIBERATELY. The criteria strings raise the sulfur level to a fractional power by writing `exp(0.125*ln(sulfurLevel))`, and MariaDB evaluates that as two transcendental calls rather than as `pow`. `power_via_exp_log` keeps that spelling. It is the same argument components/meteorology.esm makes for keeping `TK/273.15` and `273.15/TK` as separate expressions: the two spellings do not round alike, and the port's job is the arithmetic MOVES ran.\n\n`relative_power_step` AND `scaled_relative_power_step` ARE TWO TEMPLATES ON PURPOSE. The SQL writes the reference-sulfur term as `(x^g - r^g)/r^g` and the sample-sulfur term as `(m*(x^g - r^g))/r^g` -- the multiplier is INSIDE the numerator in one and outside in the other. Algebraically identical, not identical in binary64, and the corpus cannot tell them apart because it never checks this form at all. Keeping both spellings is what stops a later reader from `simplifying` a difference the reference may care about.\n\nUNITS (docs/esm-conventions.md §57). `sulfur_switch_ppm`, `sulfur_reference_ppm` and `sulfur_high_ppm` declare `ppm`; `volume_percent_scale` and `biodiesel_volume_cap` declare `percent`. §57 had left all four bare because `fuelformulation`'s property values reach a document through ONE column, `fe_propValue`, holding seven properties in seven different units -- so the column cannot be declared. The GATHERS off it can: J-FE-3 selects property 4 and J-FE-4 selects property 7, and each re-applies the unit its own property is in (§57.8). With that, the low sulfur arm's `1 - slope*(pivot - sulfurLevel)` forces `fe_expressionSulfurLowPivot` to `ppm` and `fe_expressionSulfurLowSlope` to `1/ppm`, and the biodiesel form's `min(ester, 20)/100` forces the cap and the scale to `percent`. The HIGH sulfur arm cannot be checked: it runs through `power_via_exp_log`, whose `exp(power * log(value))` has a symbolic exponent, and esm-spec §4.8.3 gives that no unit. It gets a BOUNDARY instead. `sulfur_power` divides the `ppm` out before the `log`, in the one place the two `*_relative_power_step` templates reach it, because the SQL raises the ppm NUMBER to the power and `log(429.96 ppm)` is not `log(429.96)`. This is not decoration: measured on `8ac536bf0`, `exp` and `sin` of a `degF` quantity are refused and `log` of a `degF` quantity is refused, but `log` of a `ppm` and `exp` of a `percent` are ACCEPTED -- the transcendentals check the dimension and not the SCALE that PR #339 made part of unit agreement. That is finding F52, and without the boundary this file's `ppm` declarations would be resting on it.\n\nTWO TEMPLATES THE ONROAD CHAIN ADDED, AND WHY THEY ARE HERE AND NOT THERE. `criteria_exponent` is the RUNNING-exhaust criteria polynomial -- a constant plus six `standardized_term`s over RVP, T50, T50 squared, T90, aromatic content and (capped) ethanol volume, every one of them centred at 0 and scaled by 1. That is the whole of the exponent in all 135 `generalFuelRatioExpression` rows whose `polProcessID` is 101, 201 or 301, measured: 5 distinct term sets across 13 source types, 3 fuel types and 2 model-year ranges, and the only difference between the gasoline and the E85 sets is the `least(10, ETOHVolume)` clamp, which is why the cap is a parameter and not a second template. It is NOT the whole of the exponent for the START processes 102, 202 and 302: those carry CROSS terms -- `ETOHVolume*T50`, `ETOHVolume*T90`, `ETOHVolume*RVP` and `ETOHVolume*aromaticContent` -- which `standardized_term` cannot spell, because it raises ONE property to a power. A start-exhaust rung needs a `standardized_cross_term` alongside it; no RunSpec in this repository selects process 2, so it is named rather than written. `fuel_property_or_zero` is `changeFuelFormulationNulls`, and it is the one line of this file the paragraph below used to say was unnecessary.\n\nWHAT IS NOT HERE. `changeFuelFormulationNulls` (an `ifnull(col, 0)` sweep) is a no-op against a relation whose columns are concrete -- components/fuel_effects.esm carries the five formulations it needs as literals, already filled. It is NOT a no-op against the NATIONAL `FuelFormulation` table, which onroad/model.esm reads whole: 2,118 of its 2,158 rows have a NULL `BioDieselEsterVolume`, 7 have a NULL `T50`, and a NULL reaches an `.esm` as a NaN. `fuel_property_or_zero` above is that sweep, spelled as the `value == value` NaN test `in_half_open_range` already uses. The fuel-type / fuel-supply intersection, the per-(formulation, polProcessID) de-duplication and the E85 Pseudo-THC derivation are relational steps, not arithmetic, so they live in components/fuel_effects.esm and in docs/fuel-effects-generator.md 3 rather than here.",
    "authors": ["EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"],
    "tags": ["moves", "onroad", "fuel", "generator", "template-library"]
  },
  "expression_templates": {
    "volume_percent_scale": { "params": [], "body": { "op": "const", "args": [], "value": 100.0, "units": "percent" } },
    "biodiesel_volume_cap": { "params": [], "body": { "op": "const", "args": [], "value": 20.0, "units": "percent" } },
    "sulfur_switch_ppm": { "params": [], "body": { "op": "const", "args": [], "value": 30.0, "units": "ppm" } },
    "sulfur_reference_ppm": { "params": [], "body": { "op": "const", "args": [], "value": 30.0, "units": "ppm" } },
    "sulfur_high_ppm": { "params": [], "body": { "op": "const", "args": [], "value": 303.0, "units": "ppm" } },
    "complex_model_weight": { "params": [], "body": 0.425 },

    "capped_property": {
      "params": ["value", "cap", "cap_is_active"],
      "body": {
        "op": "ifelse",
        "args": [
          { "op": ">", "args": ["cap_is_active", 0.0] },
          { "op": "min", "args": ["value", "cap"] },
          "value"
        ]
      }
    },

    "standardized_term": {
      "params": ["value", "cap", "cap_is_active", "power", "coefficient", "center", "scale"],
      "body": {
        "op": "*",
        "args": [
          "coefficient",
          { "op": "/", "args": [
            { "op": "-", "args": [
              { "op": "^", "args": [
                { "op": "apply_expression_template", "args": [], "name": "capped_property",
                  "bindings": { "value": "value", "cap": "cap", "cap_is_active": "cap_is_active" } },
                "power"] },
              "center"] },
            "scale"] }
        ]
      }
    },

    "fuel_property_or_zero": {
      "params": ["value"],
      "body": {
        "op": "ifelse",
        "args": [{ "op": "==", "args": ["value", "value"] }, "value", 0.0]
      }
    },

    "high_ethanol_property": {
      "params": ["is_high_ethanol", "substitute_value", "own_value"],
      "body": {
        "op": "ifelse",
        "args": [
          { "op": ">", "args": ["is_high_ethanol", 0.5] },
          "substitute_value",
          { "op": "apply_expression_template", "args": [], "name": "fuel_property_or_zero",
            "bindings": { "value": "own_value" } }
        ]
      }
    },

    "criteria_exponent": {
      "params": ["intercept", "rvp", "t50", "t90", "aromatic_content", "etoh_volume",
                 "etoh_cap", "etoh_cap_is_active", "coefficient_rvp", "coefficient_t50",
                 "coefficient_t50_squared", "coefficient_t90", "coefficient_aromatic_content",
                 "coefficient_etoh_volume"],
      "body": {
        "op": "+",
        "args": [
          { "op": "+", "args": [
            { "op": "+", "args": [
              { "op": "+", "args": [
                { "op": "+", "args": [
                  { "op": "+", "args": [
                    "intercept",
                    { "op": "apply_expression_template", "args": [], "name": "standardized_term",
                      "bindings": { "value": "rvp", "cap": 0.0, "cap_is_active": 0.0, "power": 1.0,
                                    "coefficient": "coefficient_rvp", "center": 0.0, "scale": 1.0 } }] },
                  { "op": "apply_expression_template", "args": [], "name": "standardized_term",
                    "bindings": { "value": "t50", "cap": 0.0, "cap_is_active": 0.0, "power": 1.0,
                                  "coefficient": "coefficient_t50", "center": 0.0, "scale": 1.0 } }] },
                { "op": "apply_expression_template", "args": [], "name": "standardized_term",
                  "bindings": { "value": "t50", "cap": 0.0, "cap_is_active": 0.0, "power": 2.0,
                                "coefficient": "coefficient_t50_squared", "center": 0.0, "scale": 1.0 } }] },
              { "op": "apply_expression_template", "args": [], "name": "standardized_term",
                "bindings": { "value": "t90", "cap": 0.0, "cap_is_active": 0.0, "power": 1.0,
                              "coefficient": "coefficient_t90", "center": 0.0, "scale": 1.0 } }] },
            { "op": "apply_expression_template", "args": [], "name": "standardized_term",
              "bindings": { "value": "aromatic_content", "cap": 0.0, "cap_is_active": 0.0, "power": 1.0,
                            "coefficient": "coefficient_aromatic_content", "center": 0.0, "scale": 1.0 } }] },
          { "op": "apply_expression_template", "args": [], "name": "standardized_term",
            "bindings": { "value": "etoh_volume", "cap": "etoh_cap", "cap_is_active": "etoh_cap_is_active",
                          "power": 1.0, "coefficient": "coefficient_etoh_volume", "center": 0.0, "scale": 1.0 } }
        ]
      }
    },

    "log_linear_ratio": {
      "params": ["exponent", "base"],
      "body": { "op": "/", "args": [{ "op": "exp", "args": ["exponent"] }, "base"] }
    },

    "biodiesel_ester_ratio": {
      "params": ["ester_volume", "coefficient"],
      "body": {
        "op": "+",
        "args": [
          1.0,
          { "op": "*", "args": [
            { "op": "/", "args": [
              { "op": "min", "args": ["ester_volume",
                { "op": "apply_expression_template", "args": [], "name": "biodiesel_volume_cap", "bindings": {} }] },
              { "op": "apply_expression_template", "args": [], "name": "volume_percent_scale", "bindings": {} }] },
            "coefficient"] }
        ]
      }
    },

    "power_via_exp_log": {
      "params": ["value", "power"],
      "body": {
        "op": "exp",
        "args": [{ "op": "*", "args": ["power", { "op": "log", "args": ["value"] }] }]
      }
    },

    "sulfur_power": {
      "params": ["sulfur_ppm", "power"],
      "body": {
        "op": "apply_expression_template", "args": [], "name": "power_via_exp_log",
        "bindings": {
          "value": { "op": "/", "args": ["sulfur_ppm",
            { "op": "const", "args": [], "value": 1.0, "units": "ppm" }] },
          "power": "power"
        }
      }
    },

    "relative_power_step": {
      "params": ["value", "reference", "power"],
      "body": {
        "op": "/",
        "args": [
          { "op": "-", "args": [
            { "op": "apply_expression_template", "args": [], "name": "sulfur_power",
              "bindings": { "sulfur_ppm": "value", "power": "power" } },
            { "op": "apply_expression_template", "args": [], "name": "sulfur_power",
              "bindings": { "sulfur_ppm": "reference", "power": "power" } }] },
          { "op": "apply_expression_template", "args": [], "name": "sulfur_power",
            "bindings": { "sulfur_ppm": "reference", "power": "power" } }
        ]
      }
    },

    "scaled_relative_power_step": {
      "params": ["value", "reference", "power", "multiplier"],
      "body": {
        "op": "/",
        "args": [
          { "op": "*", "args": [
            "multiplier",
            { "op": "-", "args": [
              { "op": "apply_expression_template", "args": [], "name": "sulfur_power",
                "bindings": { "sulfur_ppm": "value", "power": "power" } },
              { "op": "apply_expression_template", "args": [], "name": "sulfur_power",
                "bindings": { "sulfur_ppm": "reference", "power": "power" } }] }] },
          { "op": "apply_expression_template", "args": [], "name": "sulfur_power",
            "bindings": { "sulfur_ppm": "reference", "power": "power" } }
        ]
      }
    },

    "sulfur_high_multiplier": {
      "params": ["sulfur_ppm", "bracket_intercept", "power", "multiplier"],
      "body": {
        "op": "+",
        "args": [
          "bracket_intercept",
          { "op": "+", "args": [
            { "op": "*", "args": [
              { "op": "apply_expression_template", "args": [], "name": "complex_model_weight", "bindings": {} },
              { "op": "apply_expression_template", "args": [], "name": "relative_power_step",
                "bindings": {
                  "value": { "op": "apply_expression_template", "args": [], "name": "sulfur_high_ppm", "bindings": {} },
                  "reference": { "op": "apply_expression_template", "args": [], "name": "sulfur_reference_ppm", "bindings": {} },
                  "power": "power" } }] },
            { "op": "*", "args": [
              { "op": "-", "args": [1.0,
                { "op": "apply_expression_template", "args": [], "name": "complex_model_weight", "bindings": {} }] },
              { "op": "apply_expression_template", "args": [], "name": "scaled_relative_power_step",
                "bindings": {
                  "value": "sulfur_ppm",
                  "reference": { "op": "apply_expression_template", "args": [], "name": "sulfur_reference_ppm", "bindings": {} },
                  "power": "power", "multiplier": "multiplier" } }] }] }
        ]
      }
    },

    "sulfur_high_ratio": {
      "params": ["exponent", "base", "gpa_factor", "sulfur_ppm", "bracket_intercept", "power", "multiplier"],
      "body": {
        "op": "/",
        "args": [
          { "op": "*", "args": [
            { "op": "exp", "args": ["exponent"] },
            { "op": "apply_expression_template", "args": [], "name": "sulfur_high_multiplier",
              "bindings": { "sulfur_ppm": "sulfur_ppm", "bracket_intercept": "bracket_intercept",
                            "power": "power", "multiplier": "multiplier" } }] },
          { "op": "*", "args": ["base", "gpa_factor"] }
        ]
      }
    },

    "sulfur_low_ratio": {
      "params": ["exponent", "base", "sulfur_ppm", "low_pivot_ppm", "low_slope"],
      "body": {
        "op": "*",
        "args": [
          { "op": "apply_expression_template", "args": [], "name": "log_linear_ratio",
            "bindings": { "exponent": "exponent", "base": "base" } },
          { "op": "-", "args": [1.0,
            { "op": "*", "args": ["low_slope",
              { "op": "-", "args": ["low_pivot_ppm", "sulfur_ppm"] }] }] }
        ]
      }
    },

    "sulfur_switch_ratio": {
      "params": ["exponent", "base", "gpa_factor", "sulfur_ppm", "bracket_intercept",
                 "power", "multiplier", "low_pivot_ppm", "low_slope"],
      "body": {
        "op": "ifelse",
        "args": [
          { "op": ">", "args": ["sulfur_ppm",
            { "op": "apply_expression_template", "args": [], "name": "sulfur_switch_ppm", "bindings": {} }] },
          { "op": "apply_expression_template", "args": [], "name": "sulfur_high_ratio",
            "bindings": { "exponent": "exponent", "base": "base", "gpa_factor": "gpa_factor",
                          "sulfur_ppm": "sulfur_ppm", "bracket_intercept": "bracket_intercept",
                          "power": "power", "multiplier": "multiplier" } },
          { "op": "apply_expression_template", "args": [], "name": "sulfur_low_ratio",
            "bindings": { "exponent": "exponent", "base": "base", "sulfur_ppm": "sulfur_ppm",
                          "low_pivot_ppm": "low_pivot_ppm", "low_slope": "low_slope" } }
        ]
      }
    }
  }
}
